  "result": "The rule and its witnesses for LVMC_11_40_120 pass the gate (verdict OK, 14 witnesses) on the second of six runs.\n\n**Gate runs**\n1. **VACUOUS**: two leaves in the obligation moved no witness. Both were the device-closure checks inside \"the rider occupies no usable path\": `dev_governs` and the `closed_to_traffic` sign code. I added `branch_8`, `branch_9` and `branch_10`. In each, the rider rides along the roadway while also on an edge bicycle lane that is unusable: closed by a sign, closed by temporary traffic control, or only 1 m wide. A usable path lies on the same highway, so each expects violated.\n2. **OK**.\n\n**What the rule says**\n- **Applies when:** the rider (any of the three aggregates) is moving, and is on a roadway or a bicycle path of a highway. That highway must also have a roadway and a usable path.\n- **Usable path:** at least `p.usable_path_width_min` wide, and not closed by a closed_to_traffic or bicycles_prohibited sign or by temporary traffic control.\n- **Duty:** a rider on the roadway and on no usable path must be crossing a lane or the roadway, not travelling along it.\n\n**Where I departed from the plan:** the `forbid` narrative calls for an electric scooter, but I used an electric bicycle (the `permit` rider too). Under the run's reading, the `DEF-LVMC-11-02-083::electric_scooter` aggregate includes no class, and `ru.electric_scooter` is only \"unresolved\". So a rider who is only an electric scooter always has an unknown class, and `forbid` would come out unknown instead of violated. As things stand, this rule can never reach a decided verdict for an electric scooter. Someone on the planning or reading side needs to decide whether `ru.electric_scooter` should be included in that aggregate. This is written up in `task_result.md`.\n\n**Open choices I made:**\n- A lane counts for crossing as long as the rider is on it; it doesn't also have to be recorded on the same highway.\n- The witnesses give the roadway its own direction wherever the \"crossing the roadway\" branch has to decide.\n\nNo narrowings were added. Besides the three above, the extra witnesses are `branch_3` to `branch_7`: a path too narrow, a bicycles-prohibited sign, crossing and riding along a roadway with no lanes, and a stopped rider.\n\nFiles are in `library/` (paths relative to `pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/`):\n- `TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_120.lean`\n- `TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_120.lean`\n\nand in `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/LVMC_11_40_120/`:\n- `task_result.md`",
